@node Package Management
@section Package Management

@table @command
@item install [flags] @var{atoms@dots{}}
Resolve, build, install, and select one or more packages. Use
@option{--oneshot} to suppress world selection. @option{--pretend} displays the
verified plan without mutation; @option{--preflight-only} additionally validates
each planned recipe and execution policy without running build tools.
Manifest-verified @option{--fetchonly} is a bounded non-mutation operation.

@item update [flags] [@var{atoms@dots{}}]
Resolve and execute updates, defaulting to @code{@@world}.

@item uninstall @var{atoms@dots{}}
Verify and execute journaled package removal. Use @option{--pretend} for a
read-only proposal.

@item depclean [flags]
Propose orphan removal without mutation.

@item prune [flags]
Propose old-version removal without mutation.

@item deselect @var{atom}
Remove a package from @@world without uninstalling.

@item select @var{atom}
Add exactly one installed package atom to @@world using locked, state-bound
world-file mutation.

@item recover status
List durable package journals and their state.

@item recover rollback @var{id}
Roll back one active journal while holding the VDB mutation lock. Use
@option{--all-active} in place of @var{id} to recover every active journal.
@end table

@node Query and Information
@section Query and Information

@table @command
@item search [flags] [@var{query}]
Search the package database with eix-style filtering.
See @ref{Search Filters} for all available search flags.

@item installed [@var{selector}]
List installed package atoms. Versionless output is the default; selectors and
flags provide CPVs, repository, build-time, quiet, and NUL-delimited views.

@item query @var{atom}
Display metadata for a specific package.

@item state @var{subcommand}
Emit deterministic available or installed package state used by parity,
snapshot, and differential workflows.

@item info
Display system information: arise version, Go runtime, portage configuration,
active profile, and repository status.

@item equery @var{subcommand} [@var{args}]
Package queries replacing @command{equery}.
Subcommands:

@table @command
@item belongs @var{file}
Find which installed package owns a file.
@item files @var{atom}
List installed files for a package.
@item uses @var{atom}
Show IUSE and active USE flags.
@item size @var{atom}
Show total installed size.
@item check @var{atom}
Verify installed files against checksums.
@item which @var{atom}
Find ebuild path.
@item list [@var{pattern}]
List installed packages matching a pattern.
@end table
@end table

@node System Maintenance
@section System Maintenance

@table @command
@item sync
Synchronize the Gentoo repository via git (primary) or rsync (fallback), then
atomically publish the refreshed resolver index. Success means both stages
completed.

@item index
Rebuild the BadgerDB metadata database from the ebuild tree.

@item audit @var{python|perl} [--fix]
Audit installed packages for outdated Python or Perl site-packages paths.
@option{--fix --pretend} lists the affected rebuild set. Non-pretend
@option{--fix} remains gated and fails explicitly.

@item preserved-rebuild [flags]
Scan for broken shared library links and rebuild affected packages.

@item revdep-rebuild [flags]
Full reverse dependency scan for broken ELF dependencies.

@item bench
Run Arise's built-in microbenchmark report. Correctness-gated external
comparisons use the dedicated performance harness.
@end table

@node Configuration
@section Configuration

@table @command
@item dispatch-conf
List pending @file{._cfg*} config file updates in @file{/etc/}.

@item env-update
Regenerate @file{/etc/profile.env} and @file{/etc/csh.env}.

@item ldconfig
Update the shared library linker cache.

@item config @var{atom}
Run the @code{pkg_config} phase.

@item news [list|read|display]
Display Gentoo news items (GLEP 42).
@end table

