@node Search Filters
@chapter Search Filters

The @command{search} command supports eix-compatible filtering with the
following flags:

@table @option
@item --name @var{pkg}
Filter by package name.
@item --category @var{cat}
Filter by category.
@item --slot @var{slot}
Filter by SLOT.
@item --use @var{flags}
USE flag filter (leading @code{+} required, @code{-} excluded).
@item --keywords @var{kw}
Filter by KEYWORDS content.
@item --license @var{lic}
Filter by LICENSE.
@item --desc
Search in descriptions.
@item --installed
Only show installed packages.
@item --exact
Exact match instead of substring.
@item --regex
Treat patterns as regular expressions.
@item --stable
Only stable-keyworded packages.
@item --testing
Only testing-keyworded packages.
@item --sort @var{order}
Sort by @code{category}, @code{name}, @code{version}, or @code{slot}.
@item --versions
Show all available versions.
@item --format @var{fmt}
Custom output format with template variables.
@item --print @var{fields}
Print specific fields (space-separated).
@item --json
JSON output.
@item --brief
Single-line output.
@item --compact
Compact output.
@item --only-names
Output only package names.
@item --count-only
Output only result count.
@item --and
Combine queries with AND logic.
@item --not @var{pattern}
Exclude packages matching pattern.
@item --world
Only @@world packages.
@item --system
Only @@system packages.
@item --depends-on @var{atom}
Packages that depend on atom.
@item --required-by @var{atom}
Packages required by atom.
@item --has-use @var{flag}
Packages with this USE flag available.
@item --has-version @var{pat}
Packages with version matching glob.
@item --care
Show packages needing attention.
@item --overflow
Only packages with masked keywords.
@item --masked
Only masked packages.
@item --duplicates
Show all versions of each package.
@item --dump
Dump in eix-compatible format.
@end table

@node Package Flags
@chapter Package Flags

Flags available for @command{install}, @command{update}, and @command{depclean}:

@table @option
@item -1, --oneshot
Install without adding to @@world.
@item -O, --nodeps
Skip dependency resolution.
@item -o, --onlydeps
Only install dependencies.
@item -e, --emptytree
Rebuild as if nothing is installed.
@item -D, --deep
Full dependency tree.
@item -u, --update
Update to best version.
@item -N, --newuse
Rebuild on USE changes.
@item -p, --pretend
Dry run.
@item -a, --ask
Prompt before acting.
@item -q, --quiet
Minimal output.
@item -v, --verbose
Verbose output.
@item -t, --tree
Dependency tree display.
@item -j @var{N}, --jobs @var{N}
Parallel jobs.
@item -k, --usepkg
Use binary packages.
@item -K, --usepkgonly
Only binary packages.
@item -b, --buildpkg
Build binary packages.
@item -B, --buildpkgonly
Only build binaries.
@item -f, --fetchonly
Only fetch sources.
@item --backtrack @var{N}
Maximum backtracking decisions (default 20).
@item --resolver-timeout @var{duration}
Wall-clock resolver deadline (default @code{5m}). @code{0} disables the
deadline without changing the independent backtrack ceiling.
@item --approve-plan-sha256 @var{digest}
Optionally require the current plan to match this canonical verified-plan
digest, including its package state and policy fingerprint.
@item --save-plan @var{path-or-name}
Save the complete generated JSON plan for later inspection and approval.
@item --approve-plan @var{path-or-name}
Optionally require execution to match an exact saved plan after current state
and policy are revalidated.
@item --preflight-only
Validate every planned package without fetching, building, or mutating.
@item --plan-dir @var{path}
Directory used for named saved plans.
@item --journal-dir @var{path}
Directory containing durable package transaction journals.
@item --resume-file @var{path}
Path containing resumable package-action state.
@item --work-dir @var{path}
Package build and transaction workspace.
@item --fetch-jobs @var{N}
Concurrent source fetch and verification jobs.
@item --show-estimates
Show historical per-package and serial-total merge-time estimates. Estimates
are advisory and do not affect plan authorization or scheduling.
@item --complete-graph
Rebuild reverse deps.
@item --keep-going
Continue on errors.
@item --reinstall
Force reinstall.
@item --changed-use
Reinstall on USE changes.
@item --changed-deps
Reinstall on DEPEND changes.
@item --noreplace
Skip same version.
@item --exclude @var{pkg}
Exclude package (repeatable).
@item --resume
Resume last operation.
@item --skipfirst
Skip first in resume.
@item --autounmask-write
Write unmask entries.
@item --color y|n
Colored output.
@item --unordered-display
Unsorted display.
@item --load-average @var{LOAD}
Pause above load threshold.
@item --getbinpkg
Download binpkgs from binhost.
@item --getbinpkgonly
Only downloaded binpkgs.
@item --binpkg-respect-use
USE-aware binpkg selection.
@item --with-bdeps y|n|auto
BDEPEND handling.
@item --ignore-built-slot-operator-deps y|n
Ignore slot operator rebuilds.
@end table

@node Configuration Files
@chapter Configuration Files

@table @file
@item /etc/portage/make.conf
Global system configuration (CHOST, CFLAGS, USE, MAKEOPTS, FEATURES,
ACCEPT_KEYWORDS, ACCEPT_LICENSE, PORTAGE_BINHOST).

@item /etc/portage/package.use[/]
Per-package USE flag overrides. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords[/]
Per-package keyword overrides. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.license[/]
Per-package license acceptance. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.mask[/]
Masked packages (prevent installation). May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.unmask[/]
Override masks for specific packages. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/package.env[/]
Per-package environment file assignments. May be a file or directory.

@item /etc/portage/profile/package.provided
User-provided virtual packages.

@item /etc/portage/make.profile
Symlink to the active Gentoo profile.

@item /var/lib/portage/world
User-requested package list (@@world set).

@item /var/db/repos/gentoo/
Gentoo repository tree.

@item /var/db/pkg/
VDB: installed package database.

@item /var/cache/binpkgs/
Binary package cache.

@item /var/tmp/arise/
Temporary build directory.

@item /var/tmp/arise/resume
Resume state for interrupted operations.
@end table

@node Extending arise
@chapter Extending arise

arise's internal packages are organized by concern:

@table @file
@item internal/atom
Gentoo atom parser. Handles @code{>=cat/pkg-1.0:slot=[use]} syntax.

@item internal/depstring
DEPEND/RDEPEND string parser. Handles @code{||}, @code{use?}, @code{!},
@code{^^}, nested groups, slot constraints.

@item internal/ebuild
Ebuild file parser. Extracts EAPI, inherit, variables, phase functions.

@item internal/eclass
Eclass loader. Resolves inherit chains, merges variables and exported functions.

@item internal/metadata
md5-cache parser. PackageMetadata struct with EAPI 8+ fields.

@item internal/graph
Dependency graph builder. Queries BadgerDB and walks the ebuild tree.

@item internal/resolve
Backtracking dependency solver. USE, keyword, license, mask awareness.

@item internal/rebuild
Source build pipeline: verified fetch -> isolated phase execution -> image
validation -> journaled payload/VDB transaction -> lifecycle finalization.
Saved-plan approval is optional; every mutation still uses state verification,
operation locking, journaling, rollback, and lifecycle finalization.

@item internal/portage
Configuration parser. make.conf, package.use, package.accept_keywords, etc.

@item internal/profile
Profile inheritance chain parser. load parent chains, merge settings.

@item internal/binpkg
XPAK binary package read/write with USE compatibility checking.

@item internal/search
eix-style package search with 30+ filter options.

@item internal/equery
Package query: belongs, files, uses, size, check, which, list.
@end table

Coverage varies by subsystem. The maintained test lanes include unit,
adversarial, fuzz, race, differential and disposable-root integration tests;
the punch list records the remaining acceptance gates.

